  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ex-post evaluation of &quot;Support to the TVET Sector in Pakistan Project&#xbf; (TVET III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This assignment will comprise two parts:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;Part I will be the tracer study and will focus on the impact of trainings on the trainees in terms of employment and income; and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;Part II will focus on the ex-post evaluation of the whole intervention/project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The main objectives of this evaluation are to provide the relevant services of the European Union and the interested stakeholders with:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;comprehensive information contributing to an accurate assessment of the immediate and long-term value and contribution of trainings conducted during the project to the income and employability of its graduates including the uptake of self-employment opportunities (part I);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;an overall independent assessment of the performance of the &#xbf;Support to the TVET sector in Pakistan (TVET III)&#xbf;&lt;em&gt;,&lt;/em&gt; paying particular attention to its different levels of results measured against its expected objectives; and the reasons underpinning such results; and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;key lessons learned, conclusions and related recommendations in order to improve future interventions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In particular, part I of this evaluation (tracer study) will serve to assess the performance of the training component of TVET III in terms of employment, level of income and livelihood of the TVET graduates and usefulness of the training programme to them. It will also assess the usefulness of the skills of graduates of the project to the employers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Part II will serve to focus on the lessons learnt from the implementation of the action which will help in improving the implementation of the next phase.These lessons learnt can also be replicated in other EU interventions in the TVET sector in countries in the region. In addition it will also help to be accountable for the use of EU resources in relation to the results of the program and to report transparently on EU support to the TVET sector in Pakistan. It is even more relevant to assess this now as the EU has been active in the sector for more than a decade and it is therefore important to assess how effective and useful the EU&#xbf;s presence has been so far.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
